"[HEADER] Installation Infos",
"kill",
"If you haven't selected the Enemy Randomizer, when you click 'START SETUP' in the 'SETUP' tab, dark_souls_2.apworld will be installed and moved into the 'custom_worlds' folder inside the Archipelago Launcher directory. The DLL corresponding to game's version will then be downloaded into the game's 'Game' folder and will then be renamed 'dinput8.dll'.\n\nIf you have selected the Enemy Randomizer, when you click 'START SETUP' in the 'SETUP' tab, dark_souls_2.apworld will be installed and moved into the 'custom_worlds' folder inside the Archipelago Launcher directory. The 'LazyLoader' mod loader and the 'DS2Randomizer' (enemy randomizer) will be installed inside the game's 'Game' folder. The Randomizer will be transfered to the 'dllMods' folder and renamed 'randomizer.dll' and the Archipelago DLL will be installed in the 'dllMods' folder and renamed 'archipelago.dll'.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] apworld / yaml Infos",
"kill",
"DS2 is not a core Archipelago game, it needs a custom world file. When 'dark_souls_2.apworld' is downloaded in the Archipelago Folder (by clicking START SETUP), boot-up the Archipelago Launcher and go to 'Options Creator' to create your .yaml file and then, when you're done, send it to the person who will host the AP Multiworld.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"Once everything is set up, a new console window (separated from the actual game) should open when launching the game.\n\nOnce in the main menu, go to the console window (the one that launches with the game) '/connect archipelago.gg:XXXXX [slotname]'\n\nXXXXX is the room’s port. You can find this number on the website after creating a new room.\n\n'[slotname]' is the name assigned to your yaml file.\n\nFinally, you should see a text saying that you're connected and you can now go back to your game and start a new save!",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Revert Infos",
"kill",
"Without the randomizer, reverting will delete the mod DLL and the 'archipelago' folder (if present).\n\nWith the randomizer, the mod loader, enemy randomizer and the Archipelago mod will all be deleted.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] PopTracker Infos",
"kill",
"Some games have a PopTracker integration for Archipelago which allows you to track all possible Locations, Items, Upgrades, Zones, Hints and more depending on the game.\n\nFor the setup there are 3 different cases:\n\n\t• If the selected directory does not contain a PopTracker folder (or any similarly named folder), a new 'poptracker' folder will be created and the pack will be downloaded to poptracker\\packs.\n\n\t• If the selected directory already contains a folder with 'PopTracker' in its name, the installer will look for a poptracker.exe file. If one is found, the pack will be downloaded to its packs folder. If no poptracker.exe is found, the folder will be renamed to 'poptracker' and any missing files or folders will be created.\n\n\t• If the selected directory is already a PopTracker folder (for example: C:\\Users\\magni\\Documents\\poptracker), its contents will be validated. If everything is present, the pack will simply be downloaded to poptracker\\packs. Otherwise, the folder will be repaired before the pack is installed.",
"clear"

